{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1334454-free-council-techne-and-dedicated-magical-tools","id":1334454,"title":"Free Council, Techne and Dedicated Magical Tools","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-09-08T07:20:34-07:00","id":1334454,"title":"Free Council, Techne and Dedicated Magical Tools","content":"A question, given that:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Free Council are an oddity among all the other Orders.<br /> While<b> every Libertine may use complex mechanisms and systems<br /> as Order Tools</b>, the Techn\u00e9 Merit allows a Libertine to focus on<br /> a personal style of magic based on Sleeper culture, using it as<br /> an additional Tool in her magic.. </div> </div> </div>If I want to have as a Dedicated Magical Tool (Algorithms) or (Scientific Method), do I need to have the <i>Techn\u00e9 </i>merit? the<i> Broad Dedication</i> merit? None? Both?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-08T08:31:22-07:00","id":1334462,"title":"","content":"I'd say no. You do not need the merit.<br /> <br /> Techne is for things like Wicca or lucky socks or The Rules of Attraction and stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/346-troy","name":"Troy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-08T09:16:22-07:00","id":1334470,"title":"","content":"Incorrect. A Dedicated Tool is has to align with your Path and otherwise fulfill a role in as a Path Tool. Specifically quoting the book, &quot;The Dedicated tool is often the first Path tool that the mage used, or something that she grabbed at the moment of her Awakening,&quot; and that latter one doesn't quite work with the subjects presented.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/624122-techne\">Techne</a> absolutely is for Algorithims and Scientific Method as occult symbolism, though one wonders why you'd play that close when you can broaden out, particularly since Techne allows Sleepers to be involved with the process.<br /> <br /> Techne covers everything from people still trying to play the Weret Hekau's specific game book to internet mainframe structuring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-08-2019, 12:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-08T09:29:03-07:00","id":1334473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1334454-free-council-techne-and-dedicated-magical-tools?p=1334470#post1334470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incorrect. A Dedicated Tool is has to align with your Path and otherwise fulfill a role in as a Path Tool.</div> </div> </div> </div>Soul stones, Techn\u00e9 and Order Tools are all mentioned as example Dedicated Tools. Path Tools are described as the most common Dedicated Tool. I believe that any Tool Yantra (though the only explicit limit is that it has to be an item) can theoretically be dedicated. Sacraments being a natural exception due to their nature. If it were just Path Tools, then Dedicated Tools would be a subheading in that section in the core book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-08T10:01:02-07:00","id":1334480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1334454-free-council-techne-and-dedicated-magical-tools?p=1334470#post1334470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incorrect. <b>A Dedicated Tool is has to align with your Path and otherwise fulfill a role in as a Path Tool.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Not exactly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1334454-free-council-techne-and-dedicated-magical-tools?p=1334470#post1334470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Specifically quoting the book, &quot;The Dedicated tool<b> is often</b> the first Path tool that the mage used, or something that she grabbed at the moment of her Awakening,&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Emphasis mine, often, not necessarily just those. As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11887_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11887\" data-vbnamecard=\"11887\">Tessie</a> said, Soul stones and Order Tools are all mentioned as example Dedicated Tools. But I want Algorithms as a tool, it is covered by the Free Council Order Tool? does it need Techn\u00e9? does it need Broad Dedication? A combination of them?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1334454-free-council-techne-and-dedicated-magical-tools?p=1334470#post1334470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/624122-techne\">Techne</a> absolutely is for Algorithims and Scientific Method as occult symbolism, though one wonders why you'd play that close when you can<b> broaden out</b>, particularly since Techne allows Sleepers to be involved with the process.<br /> <br /> Techn\u00e9covers everything from people still trying to play the Weret Hekau's specific game book to internet mainframe structuring.</div> </div> </div> </div>Broaden out how? Can you give an example a broad use tool?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 09-08-2019, 01:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-08T10:28:39-07:00","id":1334486,"title":"","content":"I think you have it backwards. Dedicated tools may be used as Order tools, a soul stone's creator may use it as a dedicated tool, while Techne foci may be used as Order tools.<br /> <br /> A mage could replace a destroyed dedicated tool with almost anything, but from Awakening until its destruction, this tool is typical of the Path. And that's no reason not to allow it, if the symbolism is still apt (for example, computer networking is a powerful means of conquering space and mind, and us its own Hell), so long as the material aspect is kept (perhaps a USB security key).<br /> <br /> Remember, symbolism is the primary consideration for every Yantra, tools included. Symbols are realer than reality in Mage, which is why Path tools are embarrassingly symbolic, because that's how magic works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-08T10:40:18-07:00","id":1334490,"title":"","content":"Double checked the core and Signs of Sorcery, and yep, Order tools can be dedicated. My bad.<br /> <br /> On the subject of broadening out: Nutshell, can you perceive Sleeper's participating with it in a ritual casting? That's broadened out. (The Free Council does not occupy my ready Mage mind majorly, and I'm tired from some long days, so I don't readily have good examples. I might get back to it once I wake up.)<br /> <br /> I suppose the implementation of the Scientific Method as a means of ritual format, and Algorithims can be a ritual symbol everyone can work together on in a form or fashion, but it strikes me as perhaps a little unwieldy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-08-2019, 01:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-08T11:34:40-07:00","id":1334499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1334454-free-council-techne-and-dedicated-magical-tools?p=1334490#post1334490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Double checked the core and Signs of Sorcery, and yep, Order tools can be dedicated. My bad.<br /> <br /> On the subject of broadening out: Nutshell, can you perceive Sleeper's participating with it in a ritual casting? That's broadened out. (The Free Council does not occupy my ready Mage mind majorly, and I'm tired from some long days, so I don't readily have good examples. I might get back to it once I wake up.)<br /> <br /> I suppose the implementation of the Scientific Method as a means of ritual format, and Algorithms can be a ritual symbol everyone can work together on in a form or fashion, but it strikes me as perhaps a little unwieldy.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ok, but back at the original question, can I use Algorithms or the Scientific Method (or any other abstraction, as long it is within the frame of &quot;...<b>every Libertine may use complex mechanisms and systems as Order Tools</b>&quot; ) without the Techn\u00e9 merit? Or the Broad Dedication?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> FYI, an algorithm by definition is broad and potent: <i>An informal definition could be &quot;a set of rules that precisely defines a sequence of operations&quot;, which would include all computer programs, including programs that do not perform numeric calculations, and (for example) any prescribed bureaucratic procedure. </i>Perhaps someone not coming from a mathematics/computer science background might think it only relates to computer programing, but it is quite broad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 09-08-2019, 03:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-08T12:53:55-07:00","id":1334511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1334454-free-council-techne-and-dedicated-magical-tools?p=1334499#post1334499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, but back at the original question, can I use Algorithms or the Scientific Method (or any other abstraction, as long it is within the frame of &quot;...<b>every Libertine may use complex mechanisms and systems as Order Tools</b>&quot; ) without the Techn\u00e9 merit? Or the Broad Dedication?</div> </div> </div> </div>As a Yantra? Probably not. While certain weird Legacies and Nameless Orders might facilitate it, it they're basically just doing a hyper focused version of what a particular cabal in the Free Council would be pursuing as their iteration of Techn\u00e9, and denying themselves a whole bunch of resources that comes with it to boot. The Diamond Orders would see the hardcore implementation of such as getting in the way of the core elements that actually matter, and Nameless Orders and Legacies that wouldn't fall neatly into the a Free Council-esque organization would likely have similar feelings.<br /> <br /> It takes a certain kind of engagement with Algorithms and the Scientific Method to really wring the Supernal resonance out of it, and the number or organizations outside of the Free Council invested enough in getting that are increasingly small-and it's not the sort of thing you're going to get without some organizational oomph into digging into the occult value such. Mechanically speaking, Techn\u00e9 also remains the best way of articulating that sort of benefit, with other means of expressing it being ill-fit or odd angled.<br /> <br /> So, as a nutshell, you wouldn't as an individual, most organizations outside of the Free Council who would provide it are the sort of organizations that, logistically if not ideologically, have more to gain by joining the Free Council than not (which is not to say you couldn't, you would just need to have a good reason the organization on the whole presents a strong enough case to not avail themselves of limited edition lightsabers and airline tickets), and Techn\u00e9 outside of tailored Legacy Attainments is going to be the main model for it.<br /> <br /> EDIT: As a rough way of modelling this, you're effectively looking for the effects of Techn\u00e9 without being in the Free Council, unless again you really wanna dig deep and weird and make this a Legacy, which is a different subject. In the Free Council, You can get Techn\u00e9 at Status 1. In a Nameless Order that facilitates this thing, you would get the hyper-focused version of this at Status 3 <i>at best</i>, and by yourself you would need to do the equivalent work of attaining Status 5. If the Nameless Order or solitaire in question follow a train of thought more akin to the Diamond or the Seers, add 1 to those counts.<br /> <br /> Now there may be reasons to go ahead and do this, but you have to have a real knowledge of why that is.<br /> <br /> The resources and refinements on understanding that come with the (collected) centuries of experience that is made easy access to the Orders, even the Free Council, is a real and tangible benefit. It's not exactly something you can just ignore.<br /> <br /> EDIT: And yes, if you wanted to make it so any implementation of either or those worked as a Dedicated Tool, you would need Broad Dedication. If you want it as <i>just</i> a Yantra, Techn\u00e9 or a Techn\u00e9-like is needed.<br /> <br /> Out of curiosity, why are we asking?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-08-2019, 04:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-08T14:13:59-07:00","id":1334527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1334454-free-council-techne-and-dedicated-magical-tools?p=1334486#post1334486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you have it backwards. Dedicated tools may be used as Order tools,</div> </div> </div> </div>To clarify: Dedicated Tools can be used as Order Tools, <i>if</i> they also fit as an Order Tool. Just being a Dedicated Tool does not qualify as an Order Tool. On the other hand all Order Tools (that are physical items) can be dedicated to become Dedicated Tools. If you have a more abstract Order Tool (such as a practice gained through Techn\u00e9) then you need Broad Dedication.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1334454-free-council-techne-and-dedicated-magical-tools?p=1334486#post1334486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">a soul stone's creator may use it as a dedicated tool,</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. In addition to using your own soul stone, you can always dedicate someone else's soul stone as your Dedicated Tool without additional Merits.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1334454-free-council-techne-and-dedicated-magical-tools?p=1334486#post1334486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A mage could replace a destroyed dedicated tool with almost anything, but from Awakening until its destruction, this tool is typical of the Path. And that's no reason not to allow it, if the symbolism is still apt (for example, computer networking is a powerful means of conquering space and mind, and us its own Hell), so long as the material aspect is kept (perhaps a USB security key).</div> </div> </div> </div>As long as the material aspect can be said to be a part of the larger Yantra (i.e. USB security key is actually used and not just left dangling from a key chain while you work an unrelated computer network) then you should be able dedicate it just fine. If you don't have a material component, then Broad Dedication is needed.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1334454-free-council-techne-and-dedicated-magical-tools?p=1334499#post1334499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, but back at the original question, can I use Algorithms or the Scientific Method (or any other abstraction, as long it is within the frame of &quot;...<b>every Libertine may use complex mechanisms and systems as Order Tools</b>&quot; ) without the Techn\u00e9 merit? Or the Broad Dedication?</div> </div> </div> </div>You asked a few different questions all nested together so let's break it down a bit.<br /> <br /> First of all, does either fit the description of the Free Council Order Tool?<br /> This is up for interpretation and I'm not comfortable ruling one way or another. Does the text refer to systems as in organised procedures (like the scientific method), systems as in complex structures (like algorithms), or both? I can't say.<br /> <br /> If either is deemed not to fit the regular Order Tool description, can you still use them through the Techn\u00e9 Merit?<br /> Techn\u00e9 is a defined practice, and as such algorithms are immediately disqualified. You could instead use programming as Techn\u00e9. The scientific method is definitely a type of practice, but it's not its own field, if that makes sense. I would allow it if a player really wanted it, but generally say no.<br /> <br /> If they are viable Order Tool Yantras (either as regular Free Council Order Tools or Techn\u00e9 Order Tools), do you need Broad Dedication in order to dedicate them?<br /> Yes. Neither is an item, and being an item is the only explicit limit on what can be a Dedicated Tool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 09-08-2019, 05:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-08T19:10:34-07:00","id":1334567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1334454-free-council-techne-and-dedicated-magical-tools?p=1334511#post1334511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Out of curiosity, why are we asking?</div> </div> </div> </div>Part of my game, we have a Free Council Mastigos theorist, that believes that all the semiotics are just crutches, all symbols are just obfuscating true meaning, and that all the Yantras are useful just because human will works through some self-deception, therefore he wants to reap the benefits of Yantras and Dedicated Tools with pure mental exercises.<br /> <br /> The closest I imagine to that would be a combination of <i>Techn\u00e9 </i>(Some broad practice here: Rationality, Scientific Method, Algorithms??) + <i>Broad Dedication</i> (Said practice) + <i>Shadow Name</i> (Something Relevant to the Practice) + <i>Cabal Theme </i><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1334454-free-council-techne-and-dedicated-magical-tools?p=1334527#post1334527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You asked a few different questions all nested together so let's break it down a bit.<br /> <br /> First of all, does either fit the description of the Free Council Order Tool?<br /> This is up for interpretation and I'm not comfortable ruling one way or another. Does the text refer to systems as in organised procedures (like the scientific method), systems as in complex structures (like algorithms), or both? I can't say..</div> </div> </div> </div>Who could help clarify this? Has <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar14_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"14\" data-vbnamecard=\"14\">Dave Brookshaw</a> clarified what counts as a tool for a Free Councilor?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1334454-free-council-techne-and-dedicated-magical-tools?p=1334527#post1334527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If either is deemed not to fit the regular Order Tool description, can you still use them through the Techn\u00e9 Merit?<br /> Techn\u00e9 is a defined practice, and as such algorithms are immediately disqualified. You could instead use programming as Techn\u00e9. The scientific method is definitely a type of practice, but it's not its own field, if that makes sense. I would allow it if a player really wanted it, but generally say no..</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, I see the point, would agree on the Scientific Method, what about &quot;Rationality&quot; as practiced by the LessWrong community? Any broadly applicable practice?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1334454-free-council-techne-and-dedicated-magical-tools?p=1334527#post1334527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they are viable Order Tool Yantras (either as regular Free Council Order Tools or Techn\u00e9 Order Tools), do you need Broad Dedication in order to dedicate them?<br /> Yes. Neither is an item, and being an item is the only explicit limit on what can be a Dedicated Tool.</div> </div> </div> </div>This part is crystal clear. To summarise: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>IF the practice fits as a Free Council Tool, use it as is, but this is highly unlikely, therefore..</li> <li>Most likely it is needed to use <i>Techn\u00e9 </i>(the practice)</li> </ol><br /> For either case<i> Broad Dedication</i> it is required since it would not be an item, and only <i>Broad Dedication </i>allows the dedication of other Yantras<br /> <br /> <br /> Thanks for you all for your answers","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 09-08-2019, 11:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-08T21:02:06-07:00","id":1334576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1334454-free-council-techne-and-dedicated-magical-tools?p=1334567#post1334567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Part of my game, we have a Free Council Mastigos theorist, that believes that all the semiotics are just crutches, all symbols are just obfuscating true meaning, and that all the Yantras are useful just because human will works through some self-deception, therefore he wants to reap the benefits of Yantras and Dedicated Tools with pure mental exercises.<br /> <br /> The closest I imagine to that would be a combination of <i>Techn\u00e9 </i>(Some broad practice here: Rationality, Scientific Method, Algorithms??) + <i>Broad Dedication</i> (Said practice) + <i>Shadow Name</i> (Something Relevant to the Practice) + <i>Cabal Theme </i></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, on the one hand, his concept is sound. On the other hand, what he wants is Ascension.<br /> <br /> This is not a problem, just a reality.<br /> <br /> The <i>problem</i> said character would conflict against is that the Semiotics in play are there for a reason- reshaping reality by the invocation of the ideal is that it's really damn hard, and there's a reason why even the best shortcuts for such things would still basically benefit from the thousands of years of figuring out <i>how</i> to shortcut as much as possible in growing comprehension.<br /> <br /> Some kind of Techne and <i>definitely</i> Broad Dedication would definitely go a long way for it, but he would still brush up on limitations of those means as mediums for idealization, because the mediums in question can only articulate so much. At the end of day, what he really wants to master is his Gnosis and Arcana, because the art of revelation-as-action-as-revelation-as-ad-infinitum is essence of improvisational magic, with Yantras being more (very helpful) crutches to that mindset.<br /> <br /> That's not a problem either, in fact it paints a pretty clear character arc with good frustrating No Answers that still contribute to the fulfillment of a yes Answer to his story question and a lot of cool moments in the middle where he can learn from those moments where his initial crashing into walls stopped him.<br /> <br /> The various answers for getting the Techne benefit out of what he's done is also good story fodder, though I admit I still lean towards an opening arc in the Free Council. It has good drama potential, since he's really only there to get the knack of his concept down, and as he learns the limitations of that concept, the mages and cabals at the same time begin to dour on his prospect as it becomes all the more clear he's using them. It leads to a solid crux point where-in he can reinvest in the Order more wholeheartedly or invest in something else (maybe the Mysterium or Adamantine Arrow based on my limited understanding of the character, if he's interested in staying with the Pentacle, various Nameless Orders and Legacies if he doesn't ,or maybe even a solitaire if it all just chaffs him). It also leads to a nice temptation to the Seers of the Throne, because Prelates eventually <i>do</i> just shortcut all the shortcuts and plug directly in a reigning god-tyrant of reality feeding occult power and truth to their Supernal symbol.<br /> <br /> Other options, like the Nameless Orders and Legacies, would largely depend on the heretical and (borderline/possible) Left-Handed ideologies that he would taint himself with. Being a solitaire is the least appealing, because it's a lot of work that, unless the character is really well developed, amounts to a lot of empty drama that could have been resolved by just taking advantage of resources.<br /> <br /> But let's reiterate it here: Given his concept and philosophy, at the end of the day, he is eventually going to stop looking at Yantras and start looking at Gnosis and Arcana. That is where his arc clearly leads.<br /> <br /> (That said, it is a solid basis for a Legacy, whether it's valued forward or not.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-09T07:02:59-07:00","id":1334638,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> indeed that is close to what has been considered, you make far reaching points. The idea was to get the largest bang for their buck with merits, in a broad reaching way.<br /> <br /> The character admires part of the Mysterium mindset and some of their techniques (Mysteriorum Calamitas, and Mysteriorum Arche) but would never join them, too dismissive of ordinary humanity. He also admires the Adamantine Arrow for their selfless devotion (when it is aimed at humanity in general, or sleepers). Silver Ladder are seen as an ideological mirror image, close enough on their admiration of the human spirit, but distorted towards a class/caste view.<br /> <br /> Nameless are unattractive in a pure resources point of view, too limited scope to be useful.<br /> <br /> His dark passions would be truly satisfied by the Throne but serving the tyrants, the infighting, backstabbing, and the general inefficiency of it, offends him in a deep sense. If he ever goes dark, it is more likely that he becomes a corrupt Free Council/Silver Ladder member than a full member of the Seers.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 09-09-2019, 10:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-11T11:17:32-07:00","id":1335161,"title":"","content":"&quot;Algorithms&quot; is too broad a category to be a meaningful symbol in the specific case very often. It's just this side of asking for &quot;casting&quot; as a tool. The problem isn't that ephemeral things shouldn't be tools, it's that a process for finding or generating symbols should not be confused with being the effective symbols.<br /> <br /> If you allow &quot;algorithms&quot; then they should only apply to situations where the selection of or operation of algorithms <i>in general </i>are part of the action of the spell itself. That is: if you allow such a thing, no declaring a random number generator algorithm as part of casting a fate spell and turning around and hitting a life spell with an exponential growth equation, as neither of those are algorithmic processes of themselves. The specific example algorithms might apply just dandy, but neither is what was selected; If algorithms are the tool then algorithms as a concept must be the symbol that applies.... in precisely the same way one doesn't take &quot;wands&quot; as a dedicated tool and get all wands, but rather a specific wand.<br /> <br /> That said, this attempt to stretch the rules would be a perfectly reasonable research path for a character and a great justification for both of the mentioned tool merits and a nifty basis for a custom legacy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-12T09:02:47-07:00","id":1335320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thenate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1334454-free-council-techne-and-dedicated-magical-tools?p=1335161#post1335161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Algorithms&quot; is too broad a category to be a meaningful symbol in the specific case very often. It's just this side of asking for &quot;casting&quot; as a tool. The problem isn't that ephemeral things shouldn't be tools, it's that a process for finding or generating symbols should not be confused with being the effective symbols.<br /> <br /> If you allow &quot;algorithms&quot; then they should only apply to situations where the selection of or operation of algorithms <i>in general </i>are part of the action of the spell itself. That is: if you allow such a thing, no declaring a random number generator algorithm as part of casting a fate spell and turning around and hitting a life spell with an exponential growth equation, as neither of those are algorithmic processes of themselves. The specific example algorithms might apply just dandy, but neither is what was selected; If algorithms are the tool then algorithms as a concept must be the symbol that applies.... in precisely the same way one doesn't take &quot;wands&quot; as a dedicated tool and get all wands, but rather a specific wand.<br /> <br /> That said, this attempt to stretch the rules would be a perfectly reasonable research path for a character and a great justification for both of the mentioned tool merits and a nifty basis for a custom legacy.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks, understood your points. A primary question, what would be a good broad or generally applicable category for this character (specially considering what has been said about his goals)???<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And as a secondary question (I might post it as a new topic) if I wanted to use an Avatar the Airbender movement/fighting style as my dedicated tool what would be better:<ul><li>Adamant Hand (Brawl) + Broad Dedication+ Profligate Dedication (Brawl skill), OR...</li> <li>Techn\u00e9 (Martial Arts) + Broad Dedication+ Profligate Dedication (Martial Arts)</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <br /> I think that thematically Adamant Hand is a better fit, but the Yantra it provides it is only for combat, wouldn't that limit the Dedicated Tool?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 09-13-2019, 11:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-13T06:52:53-07:00","id":1335489,"title":"","content":"Why not both?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-13T07:58:55-07:00","id":1335502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1334454-free-council-techne-and-dedicated-magical-tools?p=1335489#post1335489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why not both?</div> </div> </div> </div>but will both work? I am.concerned about the adamant hand limitations","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-13T08:25:57-07:00","id":1335513,"title":"","content":"Adamant Hand allows you to make a combat action involving the chosen Skill, and the same turn apply that action as a reflexive Yantra to a spell cast on subsequent turns. Just like all Yantras the combat action needs to be linked to the spell, but if you look at the weapon Tool Yantra you see that a weapon can symbolise a lot more than just doing harm. In that regard you could make a lunge with a sword and have that symbolise the direction of the spell you cast on the next turn. Just remember that Adamant Hand is an Order Yantra which gives +1. Many people misread it and think it adds as many dice as dots in the chosen Skill, which is wrong.<br /> <br /> What's unclear to me about Adamant Hand is whether a combat action must be used in actual combat, or whether you can do a mock attack against no one and still use it as a Yantra.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 09-13-2019, 11:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts